# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Large / generated data that must never land in git history (see docs/PLAN.md §1.4,
# docs/DECISIONS.md D-006/D-012): maps, demos, replay-derived traces, connectome exports,
# training data and checkpoints all live outside the repo on the VPS. The four directory
# patterns below are anchored to the repo root (leading `/`) so they don't also match
# same-named source directories nested under crates/ (e.g. a `traces/` or `clips/` module
# folder). `secrets/` is intentionally NOT anchored (see the "Secrets" block below): it must
# also catch a stray `secrets/` directory nested anywhere, e.g. `crates/*/secrets/`.
*.map
*.demo
*.flyg
*.feather
*.parquet
*.ckpt
/traces/
/datasets/
/checkpoints/
/clips/

# Exception: small, synthetic "golden" test fixtures committed under any crate's
# tests/fixtures/ (see docs/PLAN.md §1.4) are allowed even though their names may match the
# data-file extensions immediately above (e.g. a synthetic *.map fixture). This is deliberately
# scoped to those specific extensions only, NOT a blanket `tests/fixtures/**`, so it can never
# re-allow a secret-shaped file (`.env`, `*.pem`, `*.key`, a `secrets/` dir) that happens to sit
# under a fixtures/ directory — the patterns in the "Secrets" block below are unaffected by this
# exception no matter where they match.
!crates/**/tests/fixtures/**/*.map
!crates/**/tests/fixtures/**/*.demo
!crates/**/tests/fixtures/**/*.flyg
!crates/**/tests/fixtures/**/*.feather
!crates/**/tests/fixtures/**/*.parquet
!crates/**/tests/fixtures/**/*.ckpt

# Secrets: never commit credentials, tokens or private keys. Unanchored so a nested
# `secrets/` folder (e.g. under a crate) is caught too, not just one at the repo root.
secrets/
.env
*.pem
*.key

# Local C++ oracle build output (tools/ddnet-oracle, added in a later task).
tools/ddnet-oracle/build/
__pycache__/
